      "Quotes lets you build a line-itemed quote (with discount, tax, terms, validity; line items come only from your Products catalog via 'Add product from catalog…', with the name and unit price fixed and only the quantity editable, so you can't type a one-off line or change a price on the quote; use the quote-level Discount for reductions), send it via a branded email, and the recipient views and accepts or declines (with a reason) on a public page. Quotes are numbered Q-YYYY-NNNN and move Draft → Sent → Viewed → Accepted/Declined/Expired → Paid; the detail page has Send / re-send, Edit, Mark paid, PDF download, Delete (drafts only; a sent document stays on record), and Convert to invoice (INV- numbering, no accept step). To bill without an estimate, pick Type → Invoice on the New quote page. Invoices have a 'Payment due' term (Due on receipt, Net 7/14/30/60, or No specific date) instead of 'Valid until'; both take an optional 'Billed to' organization and a billing address that auto-fills from the contact. PIPELINE LINK: in the builder you can pick the pipeline deal the quote is for — on acceptance that deal moves to its pipeline's Won stage with the quote total as value (no duplicate deal); if no deal is linked, the 'auto-create a Won deal' checkbox (default on) creates one instead. You get a push notification when a quote is accepted or declined (if you've enabled notifications), and marking a quote or invoice paid can auto-send a Google review request when that automation is on. Invoices need a payment rail connected: with Stripe connected under Settings Sub-Account → Admin tab → Payments — Stripe (agency-gated) the recipient pays by card on the invoice page and it's marked paid automatically; with a PayPal.me username (Settings → Admin tab → Payments — PayPal) the invoice shows a PayPal 'Pay' button and you mark it paid manually after the money lands. Quotes also appear on the contact's profile (Quotes card with a '+ Quote' shortcut). The assistant can list quotes and invoices (e.g. 'which invoices are unpaid?', with the outstanding total) and mark one paid when the money arrived outside the app. Sending requires Resend (email) to be configured on the deployment.",
