      "Website builds a marketing site per sub-account via gitpage.site — click Add website (or Start / Continue setup on a draft card) to open a step-by-step wizard: Start (site type, niche, quality, optional sample data) → The business → Pages & services (or Video for a funnel) → Location & hours (only when there's a contact page) → Look & feel → Your story (premium, optional) → Review & build. Next checks only the current step, the dots at the bottom show progress and jump back to finished steps, and the draft is saved after every step so closing the window loses nothing; a failed build's Try again reopens it on the review step. Choose Local (multi-page) or VSL (single-page video funnel), optionally pick a niche template (Home Services, Real Estate, Gyms & Fitness, Agency & Consulting, AI Consulting, AI Automation Agency), and click Build. Each sub-account can hold up to 5 sites. BUILD QUALITY: every site is a premium build — a studio-grade design-system build (three distinct 'design directions' to pick from per niche, or let gitpage choose), copy written by the strongest model from your facts only (nothing invented; optional Premium details for real numbers, team, testimonials and an offer), generated photography, and this workspace's own CONTACT FORM and AI CHAT WIDGET wired into the site by default. A premium build takes 10–20 minutes (brief → photography → design → publish; the card shows the current stage) and when it goes live the app automatically: creates/reuses a 'Website contact' form that feeds Contacts, allow-lists the site's hostname for Web Chat, seeds the chat bot's knowledge base from the finished site (plus a persona if none is set), switches the Web Chat bot on when the deployment has an AI key and the agency allows it, creates a speed-to-lead workflow on that form (published when SMS or email can send, otherwise saved as a draft), and pushes a 'Website published' alert — the site card lists exactly what was wired. When the workspace has Web Voice (ElevenLabs) connected, the build also switches on the chat's mic button so visitors can talk to it (untick 'Visitors can talk to the chat' on the review step to leave voice as it is). Every build is premium — there is no quick 'Standard' option. The assistant can also build a site for you from a description ('build me a gym website like fitness.com') — it can read a reference site for tone, picks the matching niche template, lists the design directions, drafts the copy, and submits the build after you confirm; it can check whether a build is done (with the stage and what was wired), and re-point a built site's call-to-action link at a form or booking page (admin; this rebuilds the site). EDITING A LIVE SITE: click Edit site on its card. It builds a copy-ready prompt for Claude (claude.ai, Claude Desktop or Claude Code) with the GitPage connector — the prompt names the exact site and tells Claude to keep the contact form and chat widget intact, preview first and publish only when you approve. The person who built the site is automatically invited by gitpage as an editor (an email arrives from GitPage), so they sign in to gitpage with that same email when connecting; step 1 in the Edit site window ('Connect GitPage to Claude') has the one-time setup. After publishing edits, click 'Update chat bot' in the same window so the chat bot learns the changes. SEO: every premium site ships with page titles and descriptions, canonical links, social-share tags, a favicon, a branded 404 page, structured business details (the right business type, opening hours, FAQ), a sitemap and a robots file; links are switched to the site's final address automatically after publishing. Each live site card reminds you to connect the site to Google Search Console (https://search.google.com/search-console) — add it there as a property and submit its sitemap (the site's address + /sitemap.xml). A custom domain is recommended before telling Google. CHAT BOT AND MULTIPLE SITES: a workspace has ONE chat bot shown on all of its websites. A 'Chat bot' badge on a site card marks the site it currently learns from (hover it for details). Each newly published site updates the bot's knowledge, and also its persona, greeting and colour where those were filled in automatically; anything you've edited yourself in AI Agents is never overwritten. One workspace should be one business — use separate sub-accounts for separate businesses. CUSTOM DOMAIN: click 'Add custom domain' under the live site's address. It shows the GitLab steps (add the domain and its DNS records, make it the Primary domain so the old gitlab.io address redirects, untick 'Use unique domain'), saves the domain in LeadStack so the chat bubble works on it, and gives a Claude prompt that updates the site's links and sitemap for search engines. Without saving it here the contact form still works but the chat bubble won't appear on the custom domain. There is no Rebuild for a live site — edit it in Claude, or delete it and build a new one (a FAILED build can be retried with Try again). Most niche templates need the business's street address (AI Consulting and AI Automation Agency don't). When agency templates are on, a live site can be saved as a template ('Save as template', agency-wide or for this client only) and new sites can start from it on the wizard's Start step. This feature is agency-gated: if Website is missing from the sidebar or shows Locked, ask your agency owner to enable it. The Website page is for sub-account admins only. If a build looks stuck, 'Re-check now' on its card asks gitpage for the latest status. Sites can be written in English, Spanish, French, German, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Polish, Czech, Romanian, Swedish or Indonesian (the 'Language' field), and local sites can include Services, Contact, Privacy policy and Terms pages. SHOP AND PRODUCT PAGES: when the workspace can sell online (see the Sell online card) and has products marked 'Sell online' with a price, a new multi-page build can also include a Shop page and one page per product with a Buy button; pick which products on the Review step under 'Products on the site' (all by default). VSL funnels don't get shop pages. Price, name and image changes made in Products update the live site within a few minutes without a rebuild; to add a product to a site that's already live, ask Claude with the GitPage connector to run add_product_pages and publish. MENU: the top menu shows up to 4 links; when a site has more pages the rest sit behind a menu button.",
