    body:
      "Workflows is a visual automation builder: pick a trigger (form submitted, contact created, tag added, deal stage changed, booking created/cancelled/rescheduled, quote accepted, quote/invoice paid, or message received — the last with an optional channel filter), then chain steps: send SMS, send AI text (only when the agency has enabled AI texts: the AI writes a personal first text from the agent persona, website knowledge and contact details following your instruction, adds 'Reply STOP to opt out' by default, waits for the agent's business hours (and won't start one in the last 30 minutes before closing), skips opted-out contacts and conversations a team member has taken over, saves a draft instead of sending when the conversation's AI mode is Suggest, keeps each text to two SMS segments, and the SMS AI agent answers the replies; a workflow with this step can't be activated until AI texts are ready), send email, send WhatsApp (approved template), wait, add/remove tag, move pipeline stage, update field, create task, internal notification, webhook, and end workflow. Two branching steps: If/else (conditions on the contact, matched ALL or ANY) and Wait for reply — 'if they don't reply within N days, do X': it takes the Replied branch the moment the contact messages back (SMS, WhatsApp, Facebook/Instagram — and email too when the two-way email inbox is enabled under Settings → Email sending domain; with the inbox off, email replies go straight to your own inbox and can't be detected) or the No-reply branch when the window ends. Each workflow has a re-enrollment setting: every time, not while already in the workflow, or only once per contact. Start from a template — Speed-to-Lead, Appointment Confirmation, Lead Nurture, Stage-Change Follow-up, No-reply Follow-up — or blank. Workflows are created as drafts; publish to make them live, and check per-run history under the workflow's Runs. Emails must include the unsubscribe link. Every workflow step (not just delays) runs through a background queue, so workflows need QStash configured on the deployment; without it, runs are marked failed and nothing sends. The assistant can list your workflows with their status, create one from a starter template (admin; as a draft, optionally pinned to one form), set a draft or paused workflow's steps and the form it listens to (admin — linear steps only: SMS, email, WhatsApp template, wait, task, notify), run a test for one contact (sends real messages), publish / pause / unpublish a workflow (admin), and flip the workspace-wide 'pause all workflows' emergency stop (admin). Related settings — the Reply-To address, sending-hours window, and the 'Pause all workflows' switch — live under Sidebar → Settings → Sending preferences (Messaging tab), not on the Workflows page. TESTING: the editor's Test button enrols one contact you pick immediately — it skips the trigger and its filters and works on a draft — but it sends REAL messages, so pick yourself or a teammate as the contact and watch the Runs tab (each run shows its status — running, waiting, completed, or failed — and the steps it took). BACKGROUND JOBS: delayed steps, wait-for-reply timeouts, booking reminders, broadcasts and voice campaigns all run through Upstash QStash; in production the app registers its own recurring jobs on QStash automatically, so there is no cron to set up on your host beyond the QStash keys. Triggers also include 'Order paid (card)' (a card payment through the workspace's connected Stripe, e.g. a Checkout page purchase or a product bought from a buy link or the website shop), and every trigger has an optional 'Only continue if' filter. Publish with the editor's Activate button (Pause stops it). The Internal notification step sends an EMAIL (subject + body) to the Agency owner, the Account contact (Settings → Admin → Account contact, falling back to the owner) or a custom address; it doesn't text or push. The 'Move pipeline stage' step sets the contact's own stage marker (used by stage audiences and If/else); it does NOT move the contact's deal cards on the Pipeline board.",
