    body:
      "The AI agents can book real appointments during a conversation instead of only sharing the booking link. Each channel books on ONE booking page: Web Chat (typed, and Web Voice when visitors talk to the chat) is set under AI Agents → Web Chat → 'Live appointment booking'; inbound phone calls under AI Agents → Voice → 'Live appointment booking'; SMS, WhatsApp and Messenger & Instagram share the page set under AI Agents → Overview → Live booking. Only published booking pages WITHOUT a deposit can be used. A channel gets booking (and moving/cancelling) only once its page is set — that's the opt-in (phone also needs the caller-changes tick to move or cancel). The AI offers up to three times from the next 7 days (web chat also shows them as buttons the visitor can tap — typed, and during a voice call, where a tap tells the agent and it carries on by voice; speaking a time still works; times offered for moving a booking show as buttons too), asks for the details it needs (web chat: name + email; web voice: name + phone or email, read back; messaging: name; phone: first name — plus a phone number for 'we call you' pages and the visit address for 'at their place' pages), tells them where the meeting happens, books, and confirms. Website and message bookings get the booking page's normal confirmation email with a calendar invite, text and reminders; phone bookings send none. MOVE/CANCEL: people texting/messaging in can move or cancel any of their upcoming booking-page appointments (recognised by number or account); phone callers can only when 'Let callers move or cancel their upcoming bookings' is ticked under AI Agents → Voice (off by default, because caller ID can be faked); website chat visitors can only change bookings made in that same chat. QUESTIONS: the Overview switch 'Ask the booking page's questions before booking' (off by default) makes every channel ask the page's intake questions first and saves the answers on the appointment. LIMITS: booking only happens while the conversation's AI is in auto mode (never suggest mode or after a team member takes over, and never on email, which is draft-only); at most 2 bookings per chat or conversation a day and 5 changes a day; an escalation keyword hands the conversation to a person first. PREREQUISITES: a saved persona (AI Agents → Overview), the channel enabled and not locked by the agency, a usable booking page; email and QStash on the deployment for confirmations and reminders. The Workspace Assistant can check all of this with an AI booking readiness report, create and publish a simple booking page for you (name, where the meeting happens, meeting length, days and hours; no deposit — deposits, team members, intake questions and styling are added later in the Booking editor), and set the booking page per channel (and the questions switch) after you confirm each step; it can't turn channels on — that's done on each channel's settings page.",
