      "Speed-to-lead means every new lead gets an instant reply and your team gets alerted within seconds. In this app it's: a Form (public page or embedded on your site) → a Workflow with the 'form submitted' trigger (starter template: Speed-to-Lead — instant SMS → email → notify the team) → a push alert on your phone. PREREQUISITES per channel: email needs the deployment's email provider (and ideally your own verified sending domain plus a Reply-To under Settings → Messaging tab); SMS needs a dedicated Twilio number under Settings → Messaging tab → SMS (or the platform's shared sender if your agency allows it); WhatsApp needs the agency gate, a WhatsApp sender, AND a Meta-approved template; every workflow step (not just delays) needs the deployment's queue (QStash) configured; push alerts need the deployment's push keys plus each teammate enabling their own devices under Your account → Notifications (iPhone: add the app to the Home Screen first). ORDER: check readiness → pick or create the form → create the workflow pinned to that form → set the steps → publish → point your website's call-to-action at the form (a site built here can be re-pointed and rebuilt; an external site links to the form's public URL or embeds the snippet) → turn on new-lead push alerts → test on yourself (the test sends real messages). THE ASSISTANT CAN RUN THIS WITH YOU: it checks readiness for every channel, lists or creates the form (with its link and embed code), creates and configures the workflow's steps, publishes it, re-points a built website's call-to-action, reports whether your push alerts are on, and runs a test — each change behind a confirmation. Branching steps (if/else, wait-for-reply) are added in the workflow editor.",
