      "Every integration is a key added to the deployment's environment (or typed into Guided setup); each lights up a specific set of features and those stay dark ('not configured') until it's set. FIREBASE — required; holds all data and logins. RESEND + EMAIL_FROM — every email: manual sends, workflows, broadcasts, quotes/invoices, booking confirmations and reminders, escalation emails (plus RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET for the two-way email inbox). OPENROUTER — every AI feature: the AI Agents on all channels, the Workspace and Agency Assistants, the Labs watchdog, AI website drafting. TWILIO — the shared env keys cover plain SMS sending; the WhatsApp sender, Missed Call Text Back, the phone dialer and the Voice agent's number all need the workspace's OWN Twilio account (Settings → Messaging tab → SMS). QSTASH (Upstash) — every workflow step and anything delayed or scheduled: workflow waits and reply timeouts, booking reminders, broadcasts, voice campaigns, social posting, daily clean-ups. VAPI — inbound Voice agent and Outbound Voice. STRIPE (deployment keys) — Client billing plans and one-time charges; a workspace's OWN card payments use its own Stripe key connected in its Settings. META app — Facebook/Instagram inbox, AI DM replies, Social Planner. GOOGLE OAUTH — Google Calendar sync. MAPBOX — the dashboard leads map. VAPID key pair — push notifications. GITPAGE — the Website builder. FIRECRAWL — the AI agents' website knowledge base and reference-site research. COSTS: there is no platform fee — each provider bills your own account at its own rates. OpenRouter is per token (the AI Agents default to Claude Haiku, a few cents per conversation; the in-app assistants default to Claude Opus, which costs many times more per message, and the owner can switch an assistant to Sonnet for lower cost), Vapi per minute of calls, Twilio per message and per minute, Resend per email beyond its free tier, QStash per message, and Firebase/hosting free tiers cover small teams. Usage limits (set on a Client billing plan, or per workspace by asking the Agency Assistant; current usage shows under Agency → Sub-accounts → Manage → Usage) cap what each workspace can consume. AUTOMATIONS_TOKEN_SECRET signs every public link (unsubscribe links in marketing emails, quote/invoice and booking links, client-billing checkout links, invites, and the Meta/Google connect flows), so it must be set.",
